{"pages":[{"w":612.0,"h":792.0,"s":[[13.889,2.206,18.17,3.8,3.431,"EQUINOX"],[13.889,5.306,14.953,1.205,1.078,"Q U A N T I T A T I V E"],[69.444,2.807,15.359,1.643,1.471,"India Equity Research"],[69.444,4.27,11.266,1.46,1.307,"10 November 2026"],[13.889,10.995,26.542,3.651,3.268,"Kalyan Jewellers"],[13.889,14.731,30.011,2.373,2.124,"Growth intact, margins on watch"],[13.889,20.845,52.931,1.809,1.634,"Kalyan reports Q2 FY27 today. The 7 October update already gave consolidated"],[13.889,22.289,52.931,1.809,1.634,"revenue growth ‘in excess of 26%’ (India c.+27%, same-store sales c.+20% on a"],[13.889,23.733,52.951,1.809,1.634,"Navratri-heavy base, Candere c.+64%), so the print is about margins, not sales."],[13.889,25.177,52.931,1.809,1.634,"We forecast revenue of ₹9,977 cr, EBITDA of ₹609 cr (6.1% margin vs. 6.3% a"],[13.889,26.621,52.964,1.809,1.634,"year ago) and PAT of ₹330 cr (+26% y/y), a little under press previews of"],[13.889,28.065,52.931,1.809,1.634,"c.⁠₹340 cr: management is steering recycled gold to 55-60% of sales and puts the"],[13.889,29.509,52.931,1.809,1.634,"dilution from exchange at 20-30bp. Its pledge to hold last year’s PBT margin in"],[13.889,30.954,52.966,1.809,1.634,"FY27 needs H2 to deliver, with Q1 at 4.4% against 5.0% in FY26; we model"],[13.889,32.421,36.652,1.809,1.634,"4.9% and sit 1-3% above consensus EPS for FY27-28E."],[13.889,34.883,52.931,1.809,1.634,"The longer case rests on three things we can measure. 1) Network: 546"],[13.889,36.328,52.934,1.809,1.634,"showrooms at end-September, with 84 Kalyan and 50 Candere openings"],[13.889,37.772,52.931,1.809,1.634,"targeted for FY27, largely franchisee-funded (FOCO stores were 234 of 354 in"],[13.889,39.216,52.964,1.809,1.634,"India at June). 2) Balance sheet: non-GML debt reached zero in Q2, ₹102 cr of"],[13.889,40.684,52.951,1.809,1.634,"non-core land is being sold and India Ratings has the company at AA-/Positive."],[13.889,42.128,52.931,1.809,1.634,"3) Returns: company-defined ROCE rose from 19.8% in FY25 to 28.8% in"],[13.889,43.572,35.948,1.809,1.634,"FY26. We forecast a 22% EPS CAGR over FY26-29E."],[13.889,46.034,52.931,1.809,1.634,"The shares are not cheap at 38x FY27E and 31x FY28E EPS. Our Dec-27 price"],[13.889,47.502,52.931,1.809,1.634,"target of ₹730 applies 32x to twelve-month forward EPS at that date, in line with"],[13.889,48.946,52.936,1.809,1.634,"the 33x paid today, so the 19% upside is earnings growth, not re-rating. That"],[13.889,50.39,52.954,1.809,1.634,"multiple needs a long runway: a ten-year FCFE DCF (12% cost of equity, 5.5%"],[13.889,51.834,52.936,1.809,1.634,"terminal growth) gives only ₹373, and today’s price implies c.23% annual profit"],[13.889,53.278,52.954,1.809,1.634,"growth over FY30-36. We rate the shares Overweight (our ladder: >15%"],[13.889,54.722,52.931,1.809,1.634,"upside). Key risks are a sharp gold-price fall or duty cut, lasting exchange-led"],[13.889,56.167,30.893,1.809,1.634,"margin dilution and a slower franchise roll-out."],[13.889,58.654,13.042,1.643,1.471,"Price Performance"],[14.778,68.023,1.489,1.022,0.915,"300"],[14.778,66.066,1.489,1.022,0.915,"400"],[14.778,64.109,1.489,1.022,0.915,"500"],[14.778,62.152,1.489,1.022,0.915,"600"],[14.778,60.195,1.489,1.022,0.915,"700"],[18.176,68.717,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Jan 26"],[22.896,68.717,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Apr 26"],[27.783,68.717,2.47,1.022,0.915,"Jul 26"],[32.669,68.717,2.96,1.022,0.915,"Oct 26"],[17.289,69.888,5.94,1.275,1.111,"KALYANKJIL ("],[23.233,69.914,0.618,1.241,1.111,"₹"],[23.846,69.888,0.303,1.275,1.111,")"],[26.93,69.888,7.901,1.275,1.111,"NIFTY 50 (rebased)"],[20.381,71.048,1.972,1.387,1.209,"YTD"],[25.74,71.048,1.433,1.387,1.209,"1m"],[30.19,71.048,1.433,1.387,1.209,"3m"],[34.446,71.048,1.984,1.387,1.209,"12m"],[15.277,72.114,1.691,1.387,1.209,"Abs"],[19.462,72.114,2.811,1.387,1.209,"26.4%"],[24.269,72.114,2.811,1.387,1.209,"10.3%"],[29.271,72.114,2.26,1.387,1.209,"1.2%"],[33.527,72.114,2.811,1.387,1.209,"19.6%"],[15.492,73.179,1.476,1.387,1.20